  "_about": "Coordinates for every covered location. Readings come from Open-Meteo's air quality API, which is free, needs no key, and serves CAMS global reanalysis interpolated to a point. That last part is what makes covering all of NCR honest: it is a modelled field rather than a nearest-station lookup, so Bahadurgarh gets a number computed for Bahadurgarh instead of Delhi's monitor pretending to speak for it.",
